.TH EYFF 1 "@DATE@" "eyff @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eyff \- explore Your F*cking Files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eyff
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-completions
.IR shell ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eyff
explores your files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-completions " " \fIshell\fR
Print the completion script for
.IR shell ,
which is
.BR bash ,
.B zsh
or
.BR fish ,
and exit. For example:
.B source <(eyff \-\-completions bash)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Read the config from
.I file
instead of the default ones.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/eyff/config.lua
.RI ( ~/.config/eyff/config.lua
if XDG_CONFIG_HOME is not set)
The config, unless
.B \-\-config
gives another one. If it doesn't exist, the defaults are used. A
.I config.lua
in the current directory is only read when given with
.BR \-\-config :
being Lua, a config can run commands.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config is a Lua 5.4 file that defines a
.B Config
table. Every field is optional:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Config = {
}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the arguments or the config are wrong.
.SH AUTHOR
Hugo Coto <hugocoto100305@gmail.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lua (1)
